{
  "description": "Database pool with request classes under a page-read flood, at the engine-input level (docs/simulation.md, Fixtures). A pool of 20 connections with classes money (reserved 2), moves (reserved 6) and page-reads (limit 3, bound 50) sits in front of 4 FIFO I/O channels with a USL demand factor; every query holds its connection while it uses the I/O. Base: a page-read flood of 5,000/s from 2 s to 6 s over 1,000 moves per second; control: page reads at 50/s. The claim is the p99 of the database leg of a move (pool wait plus I/O) within 30 ms over the flood window. Twins: collapse-classes on the pool, and the page-read limit raised to 12; each must fail the claim in the base and hold in the control. Every number is assumed and sized so that a run stays short: the fixture tests the engine, the metrics and the claim method, and is not evidence about any system.",
